From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: ubi: skip rootfs auto-attach for embedded initramfs

An embedded initramfs already supplies the active root filesystem.
Attaching the persistent partition named "ubi" during the late initcall is
not needed in that boot mode. It can also start the UBI background thread
before userspace can apply a RAM-boot safety policy.

Keep the normal flash kernel behavior unchanged. OpenWrt's regular kernel
has an empty CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE and continues through
ubi_auto_attach(). The separately built initramfs kernel has a non-empty
source list, so it leaves all persistent UBI partitions detached from the
first userspace instruction.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@local>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
@@ -1279,6 +1279,13 @@ static void __init ubi_auto_attach(void)
 	size_t len;
 	char magic[4];
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE
+	if (CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE[0] != '\0') {
+		pr_notice("UBI: skip auto-attach for embedded initramfs\n");
+		return;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	/* try attaching mtd device named "ubi" or "data" */
 	mtd = open_mtd_device("ubi");
 	if (IS_ERR(mtd))
